<%# === Pain Grid — "The Reality of Modern Automation" === %>
<section id="pain-points" class="border-b border-slate-800">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <h2 class="mb-16 max-w-2xl">The Reality of Modern Automation</h2>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-x-8 gap-y-16">
      <div class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-4xl text-slate-700 mb-4">01</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2">Brittle by Default</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Most automation is built to demo, not to withstand three years of undocumented edge cases.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-4xl text-slate-700 mb-4">02</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2">Invisible Failure Modes</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Systems fail silently long before anyone notices — usually in the process nobody is watching.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-4xl text-slate-700 mb-4">03</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2">Single Points of Failure</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-400">One vendor, one script, one integration — and the entire operation depends on it holding.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-4xl text-slate-700 mb-4">04</p>
        <h3 class="mb-2">No One Owns the Risk</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Automation gets built by whoever had time, not whoever was accountable for what happens when it breaks.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

